  pxC_t: "Rule 3 · Winner-take-all districts (the gerrymander test)",
  pxC_p: "Slovenia does not use districts for referendums — so how much would a district map matter? Build 88 equal-size districts from precincts and draw them as favourably as possible for the losing side: where the vote is near parity (RTV fee 51.7%, investigations law 50.5% of election-day votes) the loser reaches 45 districts of 88 — a majority. Against a 60.5% defeat even the best map manages only 17.",
