  pxD_p: "For the binding investigations referendum the Constitution sets two locks on rejection: a NO majority, and NO votes from at least 1/5 of all registered voters. NO cleared both — by 132,971 over the quorum. But the quorum counts people who did not vote: with 664,854 more registered voters (+39%), the same 472,444 NO votes would miss 1/5 — the law would stand, without a single ballot changing.",
