  m1_d: "What it checks: stuffed ballot boxes push precincts out to the right of the turnout curve and concentrate extra votes for one side there. The method fits a smooth bell to the turnout distribution, finds where the honest decline ends (the 70.1% line, read off the three other referendums, which share the same precincts and electorate), and counts the votes beyond it. In all four referendums the anomalous zone holds 4,135–4,651 YES votes (0.89–1.00% of each YES total) and 1,297–1,812 NO votes (0.41–0.45%) — the right edge of the same city/countryside gradient, not a separate cluster; deleting it would shift any outcome by at most 0.15 points.",
