  m2_d: "What it checks: ballot-stuffing ties high turnout to high result — on falsified data a separate “tail” of 80–100%-turnout precincts stretches toward 80–95% results while the rival’s share collapses in exactly those precincts. Here the cloud is one continuous body: the YES share rises smoothly with turnout (+4 points per 10 points; weighted correlation +0.27…+0.38), with no kink at the right edge. Above 80% turnout sit only 10 tiny precincts — 0.1% of ballots.",
  m2_c1: "Parliamentary Investigations Act: turnout × YES share, weighted correlation +0.36 — one smooth gradient.",
  m2_c2: "Social assistance: +0.35; the gradient is the city/countryside split, not a fraud tail.",
  m2_c3: "Local voting rights: +0.38 — the steepest of the four, still a single continuous cloud.",
