  m2_a4: "Turnout vs YES share scatter, RTV fee: one continuous cloud, no separate tail",
  m3_d: "What it checks: Klimek et al. (PNAS 2012) model precincts as a mix of two 2D clusters in the turnout × result plane; in falsified elections the second cluster is compact and sits at 80–100% turnout with high results. The formal criterion fires here as well, but both components lie at mid-range turnout (51–56%) — a gradient inside one continuous cloud, identical in all four referendums (share correlations 0.94–0.96). The classic fraud island at 80–100% turnout does not exist: above 85% only two precincts remain (19 and 21 voters).",
  m3_c1: "Parliamentary Investigations Act: 2nd-component weight 0.42; both clusters at mid-range turnout — no fraud island.",
  m3_c2: "Social assistance: weight 0.49. The “second cluster” is the rural, YES-leaning half of one gradient.",
  m3_c3: "Local voting rights: weight 0.48 — the same picture.",
  m3_c4: "RTV fee: weight 0.43; the density above 80% turnout is empty.",
