  m4_d: "What it checks: numbers typed in by hand cluster at round values — a turnout or result ending exactly at a whole percent (or a multiple of 5) should be rare. The test compares the share of precincts with integer values against a Monte Carlo null built from the same data. Every statistic lands within ±1.3 (turnout z −0.0…+0.4; YES share z ≤ +1.1; NO share z ≤ +1.3): no handwriting signature. Honest caveat: with ~460 voters per precinct the test detects only mass falsification — quantified in the self-test below.",
  m4_c1: "Parliamentary Investigations Act: integer turnout z = 0.0, multiples of 5 z = −0.1, YES share z = +1.1 — all within noise.",
  m4_c2: "Social assistance: turnout z = +0.4; YES share z = +0.4.",
  m4_c3: "Local voting rights: turnout z = −0.0; YES share z = +0.2.",
  m4_c4: "RTV fee: turnout z = +0.2; YES share z = +0.2.",
  m4_a1: "Integer-percentage peaks, parliamentary investigations act: observed bars match the Monte Carlo null",
